  <iati-identifier>XI-IATI-EC_NEAR-2022-ACT-61256</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XI-IATI-EC_NEAR" secondary-reporter="0" type="15">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">European Commission - Directorate-General for Neighbourhood and Enlargement Negotiations</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reducing vulnerabilities and enhancing food security through support to conflict affected populations and agricultural production in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the action is to mitigate the impact of Russia&#xBF;s war of aggression on Ukraine&#xBF;s population (by strengthening the means of the Government) (overall objective). It will do this by supporting the livelihoods&#xBF; needs of conflict affected populations, by strengthening the capacity of Ukraine&#xBF;s legitimate public institutions, protecting cultural heritage, contributing to ensuring housing for IDPs and returnees and continuity of education through the repair of 74 school buildings (since, in view of the approaching winter, this has become an important priority of the Government of Ukraine). The action will also contribute to Ukraine&#xBF;s food security and economic resilience by ensuring uninterrupted production of agricultural and food products and supporting the access of farms (i.e. legal entities and individual agricultural producers) to working capital (specific objectives). The Action therefore directly contributes to SDG 1 on ending poverty in all its forms everywhere and SDG 2 - Zero hunger; SDG 3 - Good health and well-being; SDG 4 - Quality education; SDG 5 - Achieve gender equality and empower all women and girls; SDG 6 - Clean water and sanitation; SDG 9 - Industry, Innovation and Infrastructure; SDG 10 Reduced inequalities and not least SDG 16 - Peace, justice and strong institutions. The Action primarily contributes to priority 5 of the 2021-2027 Multiannual Indicative Programme relating to resilient, fair and inclusive societies. The Action further supports the Economic Recovery Plan for Ukraine, the past ongoing and upcoming emergency Macro Financial Assistance (MFA), and budget support already delivered in March, April and September 2022.</narrative>
  </description>
